  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) This paper proposes a simple, automatable late-stage radiofluorination strategy in which no-carrier-added [18F]fluoride directly converts α-bromo-α-fluoroalkane precursors into high-molar-activity 18F-labeled α,α-difluoromethylalkanes, addressing limitations of prior approaches and expanding PET tracer chemical space.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
  "NROOT_COMMON" [label="(0,0,0) When PET radiochemistry has both a strong need for high-molar-activity 18F-labeled motifs and practical limitations in existing routes, a direct late-stage [18F]fluoride substitution strategy on suitable precursors is a meaningful research proposal for expanding tracer-accessible chemical space."];
  "R4" [label="(0,0,0) Recognition that difluoromethyl groups can confer distinct advantages in biomolecule design supports increased interest in methods for incorporating the α,α-difluoromethyl group."];
